      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the usual maximum for adults:\n- The immediate-release maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- A single dose of 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day). The \"1700\" may be a mix-up with 850 mg \u00d7 2 tablets, or with a 1,700 mg total daily dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or frequency**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
